I would make one more architectural improvement

Instead of every detector returning a different type, define a common detector interface such as:

export interface DetectorResult<T> {
    detector: string;
    success: boolean;
    data: T;
    warnings: string[];
}

Then every detector—whether it's MetadataDetector, FrameworkDetector, or GitDetector—returns the same envelope. ProjectAnalyzerService only has to merge the data from each detector while still preserving warnings. This consistency becomes especially valuable when you later add parallel execution, caching, telemetry, or plugin-based detectors.

